# AfroTransact local secrets: your own provider credentials for a real local test.
#
#   mkdir -p .local && cp infra/local/secrets.env.example .local/secrets.env    # .local/ is gitignored
#   $EDITOR .local/secrets.env                                                 # fill in what you have
#   make secrets-check                                                         # what is set, missing, malformed
#   make up                                                                    # local.sh sources the file
#
# tools/dev/local.sh sources this file (set -a) on `up`, `restart <svc>` and `mobile`, so every service, web app and
# Expo app it starts gets these variables; a value here wins over the same variable in your shell. Change a value,
# then `tools/dev/local.sh restart <service>` (Expo: `make down` + `tools/dev/local.sh mobile`: Metro inlines
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* when it bundles).
#
# Shell syntax: KEY=value, no spaces around =. Quote values with spaces or special characters in single quotes.
# Multi-line values (PEM keys, JSON) go in single quotes across lines. Leave a line empty or commented to use the
# local fallback. TEST-MODE KEYS ONLY: the checker warns on sk_live_/pk_live_ and payments refuses live keys locally.
#
# Full reference (what each powers, where to create it, webhooks, deployed secret-store paths):
# docs/engineering/secrets-and-configuration.md
#
# Everything internal (database passwords, signing keys, service client secrets) has a committed local default:
# nothing to set for those.

# ── Stripe (payments, seller, gateway-bff) — REQUIRED for checkout ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dashboard → (Test mode on) → Developers → API keys. Both keys from the SAME account.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# `stripe listen --forward-to localhost:8105/v1/webhooks/stripe` prints "Your webhook signing secret is whsec_…".
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Optional, seller onboarding (Connect) and plan billing webhooks: a second / third `stripe listen`; the events for
# each endpoint are listed in docs/engineering/secrets-and-configuration.md (Stripe → Deployed).
STRIPE_CONNECT_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
STRIPE_BILLING_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ── Twilio (notifications) — SMS: sign-in codes, order and delivery texts ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Console → Account Info: Account SID (AC…) and Auth Token. Then a sender: a Twilio number (E.164) or a Messaging
# Service SID (MG…). Without these: texts are logged and identity's one-time codes go to Mailpit.
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
TWILIO_FROM=
TWILIO_MESSAGING_SERVICE_SID=
# Optional: a public tunnel URL for notifications (cloudflared/ngrok to localhost:8208) so Twilio can post delivery
# status callbacks. Leave empty locally: no callbacks, sending still works.
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=
# Optional: the bootstrap admin's phone (E.164) for staff sign-in codes; only used when the admin is first created.
BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PHONE=

# ── Resend (notifications) — email to real inboxes ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# resend.com → API Keys → Create (Sending access). Without it: every email goes to Mailpit http://localhost:8025.
RESEND_API_KEY=
# REQUIRED with Resend: an address on a domain verified in Resend (Domains), or onboarding@resend.dev, which only
# delivers to the email address of your own Resend account.
EMAIL_FROM='AfroTransact <onboarding@resend.dev>'
EMAIL_REPLY_TO=

# ── Search engine — Elasticsearch (default) or Meilisearch ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SEARCH_PROVIDER=meilisearch starts Meilisearch (http://localhost:7700) instead of Elasticsearch and points search and
# indexer at it; run tools/dev/local.sh restart search indexer after changing it. Both read the same variable, so they
# always agree. After switching, re-run the indexer backfill: the new engine starts empty. docs/engineering/search-providers.md
SEARCH_PROVIDER=elasticsearch
#MEILISEARCH_URL=http://localhost:7700
#MEILISEARCH_API_KEY=local-meili-master-key

# ── OpenRouter (ai-gateway) — Lola assistant, semantic search, AI moderation ───────────────────────────────────────
# openrouter.ai → Keys → Create Key (sk-or-v1-…). ai-gateway starts with make up; after adding the key run
# tools/dev/local.sh restart ai-gateway. Every AI task defaults to the cheapest models (Gemini 2.5 Flash-Lite, then GPT-5 Nano);
# raise one with e.g. AI_MODELS_CHAT=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.5 (tasks: INTENT, PLANNING, CHAT, LISTING_WRITER,
# TRANSLATION, TRIAGE, IMAGE_MODERATION). docs/runbooks/cost.md.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
#AI_MODELS_CHAT=

# ── Social sign-in (identity) — optional; a provider's button appears only when its pair is set ────────────────────
# Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials → OAuth client ID (Web application);
# redirect URI http://localhost:8100/login/oauth2/code/google
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Apple Developer → Identifiers → Services ID; the secret is a JWT you sign with a Sign in with Apple key (.p8).
# Apple does not accept localhost return URLs: needs a tunnel with HTTPS.
APPLE_CLIENT_ID=
APPLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# developers.facebook.com → My Apps → Create App → Facebook Login; App settings → Basic: App ID / App Secret.
FACEBOOK_CLIENT_ID=
FACEBOOK_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── Mobile (Expo; inlined at bundle time) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Defaults to STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY (local.sh copies it); set only to use a different key in the app.
EXPO_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
EXPO_PUBLIC_STRIPE_MERCHANT_ID=

# ── Maps / geocoding (geo) — optional; without a key local uses fixtures + OpenStreetMap ──────────────────────────
# Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → enable Places API (New) (+ Geocoding API, Routes API) → Google Maps Platform
# → Keys & Credentials → API key. Restrict it by API; HTTP referrers don't work (geo calls Google server-side), so
# Application restrictions = None (or your IP) locally. Either variable makes Google Places the only autocomplete
# provider; GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY wins when both are set. See docs/engineering/secrets-and-configuration.md.
GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=

# ── Carriers (carrier-gateway, sandboxes) — optional; see docs/runbooks/carrier-sandboxes.md ───────────────────────
# Without credentials, local uses the test carrier for USPS, UPS, FedEx and DHL: test rates, PDF labels marked TEST,
# tracking that reaches delivered within 15 minutes. Set a carrier's credentials to use its real sandbox instead.
UPS_CLIENT_ID=
UPS_CLIENT_SECRET=
UPS_ACCOUNT=
USPS_CLIENT_ID=
USPS_CLIENT_SECRET=
USPS_PAYMENT_TOKEN=
FEDEX_CLIENT_ID=
FEDEX_CLIENT_SECRET=
FEDEX_ACCOUNT=
DHL_USERNAME=
DHL_PASSWORD=
DHL_ACCOUNT=

# ── Product data and demo photos — optional ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GS1 (catalog): Verified by GS1 API key; also set GS1_ENABLED=true.
GS1_API_KEY=
# GS1_ENABLED=true
# make seed photos: pexels.com/api (key) and unsplash.com/developers (Access Key); else Wikimedia Commons.
PEXELS_API_KEY=
UNSPLASH_ACCESS_KEY=

# ── Push and WhatsApp (notifications) — optional; without them these messages are logged ──────────────────────────
# Firebase console → Project settings → Service accounts → Generate new private key (paste the JSON in single quotes).
FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=
# Apple Developer → Keys → + (Apple Push Notifications service) → download the .p8 once; Key ID and Team ID.
APNS_KEY_P8=
APNS_KEY_ID=
APNS_TEAM_ID=
# Meta for Developers → WhatsApp → API Setup: temporary or system-user access token and the phone number id.
WHATSAPP_TOKEN=
WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=

# ── Error monitoring (Sentry) — optional ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# sentry.io → Project → Settings → Client Keys (DSN). One project per app is typical.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
SENTRY_DSN=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
